fix(maintenance): nightly clean of containers, brew/npm/uv caches

A hub at 97% full held 25.7 GB of exited gate test containers, 8.6 GB
of Homebrew cache, 5.5 GB of npm cache and 82 GB of uv cache: the
docker prune runs Sundays only, no job cleaned brew or npm, and
uv-prune ran only from the login agent, which an always-on hub never
runs again.

run now removes exited containers (created ones stay), runs
brew cleanup -s and npm cache clean --force (skipped while npm runs),
both bounded, and runs uv-prune in a subshell. A uv prune skipped
three nights in a row is a finding with a key that keeps one report.
check lists each would-be removal.

Closes: sd:8746
